  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Raising Voices, Creating Opportunities - II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Vietnam):  .Raising Voices, Creating Opportunities - II (RVCO-II) Activity works to improve Disability Policy Implementation in targeted provinces in Vietnam to promote disability rights and expand opportunities for inclusion of persons with disabilities (PWDs). ..RVCO-II works with national counterparts to improve policies for persons with disabilities and build capacity of local government/actors to implement disability policies. RVCO-II contributes to the revision of the Disability Law will help ensure equity and non-discrimination against persons with disabilities. By supporting the monitoring network and facilitating the National Disabilities Action Plan implementation at the provincial level, RVCO-II helps to fulfill Vietnam&apos;s commitment to the convention on the rights of persons with disabilities. With FY 2021 funding, RVCO-II will provide technical assistance on the Alternative Report to support the implementation of the UN Convention on Protecting the Rights of PWDs...RVCO-II also provides direct assistance, including disability equity training, reproductive health checks for women with disabilities, and legal counseling services for PWDs in Quang Tri, Thua Thien - Hue, and Quang Nam provinces. Its continued advocacy efforts on physical access, independent living, and disability rights will help promote a better understanding of disability issues and facilitate the social inclusion of persons with disabilities..This activity implements Congressional directives and the policy priority to address war legacies to advance the bilateral relationship. By improving disability policies and providing direct services to PWDs, the activity contributes to the achievement of the Mission&apos;s objectives of promoting greater social, economic, and political opportunities for the most vulnerable populations, including those suffering from war-related disabilities. . .</narrative>
  </description>
